                <pb facs="0488" n="404" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg404"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Powell to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Santo Domingo City</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-11-05"><hi rendition="#italic">November 5,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 641, Santo Domingo Series.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform the Department
                    that the United States naval vessel <hi rendition="#italic">Baltimore</hi>,
                    Commander Briggs, arrived here this morning at 7 o’clock, and left for Samana
                    Bay to convoy the steamship <hi rendition="#italic">Cherokee</hi>, and if she
                    has left will proceed to Puerto Plata.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. F. Powell.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
